  body: "# Student partner income and family attribution\n\n## Authored interpretation\n\nThe captured
    guidance says student applies to the individual rather than the family and describes treating a student
    partner’s income as the claimant’s after calculating its weekly amount.\n\n## Scope and exceptions\n\
    \nThis is a scoped source attribution sequence, not a decision that every student payment counts.
    Student-income calculation, disregards, children, the benefit involved and transitional rules remain
    dependencies. Do not transplant the sequence into UC, Pension Credit or a calculator without further
    evidence.\n\n## Inspected source passages\n\n- [DMG 30015, PDF page 7](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/660bd8e238f66c001184a8db/dmgch30.pdf#page=7)
    — DMG Vol 6 Ch 30: Students, young claimants and their partners.\n\n## Evidence and review status\n\
    \nModel-assisted interpretation of selected passages in the 15 September 2026 frozen source snapshot.
    Specialist review is required. Source acquisition, source revision, legal effective dates and this
    record’s authoring time are separate.\n\nThis is an independent experimental publication, not an official
    DWP document, individual advice, an entitlement decision or an executable rule. Machine-extracted
    text may alter reading order, footnotes and characters. No PDF visual inspection, whole-chapter coverage
    or behavioural evaluation pass is claimed by this record.\n\n- `dmg-vol6-ch30`: PDF SHA-256 `1540b54680884fdaa8a71e26fdebe12899d876b459d448198a7c941a37960780`;
    extracted pages SHA-256 `768537aba8259637b2425c4f5359b19a59adee89282078ead1e22f6c4f973665`.\n"
  semantic_relations:
  - target: term/jsais-family-income-attribution
    predicate: http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related
    rationale: The student paragraph explicitly separates the individual student from family
      membership and identifies when partner income is attributed.
    evidence:
    - page: page/dmg-vol6-ch30/0007
      quote: "30015 A reference to a student is a reference to that person alone. It does not include
        the student's\npartner or a child or young person. But for JSA(IB) and IS if the student is the
        claimant's partner, the\n\nstudent's income is treated as the claimant's1. This happens once the
        weekly amount to be taken into\naccount has been worked out.\n\n\n                           \
        \                                           1 JS Act, s 13(2); SS CB Act 92, s 136(1)"
      locator: DMG 30015
